TITLE: YGGDRASIL A41 / T8Y — Veteran-Core Recruitment Exclusion Field
DATE: 2026-09-22
STATUS: PREREGISTERED POPULATION-TURNOVER EXPERIMENT / NON-CANONICAL
TRACK: YGGDRASIL TRAINING T8Y / APPLICATION-A
PARENT: A40 Subtractive Support-Credit Pressure
MECHANISM PARENT: A36 Spatially Cooperative Protected Hedge Niches
BRANCH: dg1a-ar

PURPOSE

A40 established that SUBTRACTIVE support credit
creates real local erosion ordering
without the balanced false-majority
or true-reversal inertia of ZERO_CROSS_SLOW.

But A40 did not break the biased-periodic oscillator.

Therefore A41 moves exactly one causal level outward.

Committed-cell defection remains frozen
at A40 SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW.

A41 changes only how currently uncertain U cells
are recruited around surviving committed cores.

QUESTION

Is the remaining periodic attractor
being regenerated by population turnover
around a locally surviving core?

Can veteran committed cells
use their accumulated evidence depth
to inhibit nearby recruitment
to the opposing side
without preventing genuine reversal?

F41 FREEZE

Let the exact A41 implementation freeze commit be F41.

No real A41 world,
population outcome,
or scientific result
may be derived before F41 exists.

WORLD SHAPE

384 fresh post-F41 trials.

48 contexts x 8 replicas.

48 cells.
48 epochs.

Environmental families remain structurally identical
to A40.

PARENT ORGANISM

Use the full A36 organism unchanged:

A29 pulse ecology;
A30 local nonlinear cross-inhibition;
A31 refractory memory;
A34 contradiction-suppressed independent recruitment;
A35 protected H uncertainty phenotype;
A36 spatial H niche entry/release cooperation.

No A37 lineage state exists.

COMMITTED-STATE LAW

All A41 arms use A40 SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW
for committed-state defection.

rho = 3/4.

For a C-committed cell:

M_pre = max(0,B_pre).

For an S-committed cell:

M_pre = max(0,-B_pre).

PRESSURE = max(0,L_op-M_pre).

p_stay = 1/(1+(PRESSURE/(1/2))^3).

No change is permitted
to the committed-state defection law.

BASE RECRUITMENT

Preserve A40 / A34 base rates:

sup_C = .75 * pool_C + .25 * local_C;
sup_S = .75 * pool_S + .25 * local_S.

oppx_C = .75 * pool_S + .25 * local_S;
oppx_S = .75 * pool_C + .25 * local_C.

g_C = 1/(1+(oppx_C/(1/2))^3).
g_S = 1/(1+(oppx_S/(1/2))^3).

lambda_C = ETA * sup_C * g_C.
lambda_S = ETA * sup_S * g_S.
lambda_H = ETA * sup_C * sup_S.

ETA = 1/2.

H recruitment is unchanged in every arm.

CORE SNAPSHOT TIMING

For recruitment at epoch t:

1. capture B_pre at epoch start;
2. update signed B as in A40;
3. execute H release;
4. execute committed-state defection using A40 SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW;
5. form a frozen survivor-core snapshot;
6. execute U-cell recruitment.

A cell contributes to the core field
only if it is still C or S
after the epoch's defection decisions.

For margin weighting,
the surviving cell contributes
its state-aligned M_pre
from the beginning of that epoch.

Thus current adverse evidence
is not counted twice
against the same veteran support credit.

CORE RADIUS

Use exactly the existing recruitment radius:

R_core = RECRUIT_R = 3.

No new radius exists.

OCCUPANCY FIELD CONTROL

For an eligible U cell i:

Q_C_occ(i)
=
mean over radius 3
of 1[state_j = C].

Q_S_occ(i)
=
mean over radius 3
of 1[state_j = S].

Then:

lambda_C'
=
lambda_C * (1 - Q_S_occ).

lambda_S'
=
lambda_S * (1 - Q_C_occ).

lambda_H is unchanged.

This tests spatial incumbent exclusion
without evidence-depth weighting.

VETERAN-MARGIN FIELD

For an eligible U cell i:

Q_C_margin(i)
=
mean over radius 3
of 1[state_j = C] * max(0,B_pre_j).

Q_S_margin(i)
=
mean over radius 3
of 1[state_j = S] * max(0,-B_pre_j).

Then:

lambda_C'
=
lambda_C * (1 - Q_S_margin).

lambda_S'
=
lambda_S * (1 - Q_C_margin).

lambda_H is unchanged.

Because 0 <= M_pre <= 1,
both Q fields remain in [0,1].

No gain,
scale,
offset,
threshold,
or fitted parameter is added.

INTERPRETATION

A surviving C veteran core
suppresses nearby S recruitment.

A surviving S veteran core
suppresses nearby C recruitment.

The field does not force same-side recruitment.

It only prevents a short counter-pulse
from rebuilding an opposing population
too easily in the immediate neighborhood
of a surviving core.

ARMS

Exactly six arms.

D2:
D2_BASE_SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW;
D2_OCCUPANCY_EXCLUSION;
D2_MARGIN_EXCLUSION.

D3:
D3_BASE_SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW;
D3_OCCUPANCY_EXCLUSION;
D3_MARGIN_EXCLUSION.

The BASE arm is the A40 SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW mechanism
with recruitment unchanged.

No additional rho,
radius,
gain,
or threshold arms are permitted.

PRIMARY TARGET

Biased-periodic contexts:

44;
45;
46;
47.

Report oscillation separately
for each context.

BALANCED CONTROL

Contexts:

40;
41;
42;
43.

Report:

oscillation;
final majority;
false-majority rate;
no-majority occupancy.

A41 must not solve pulse chasing
by manufacturing a persistent majority
under genuinely balanced evidence.

RECRUITMENT-BOUNDARY MECHANISM MEASUREMENTS

At every biased-periodic adverse-pulse epoch,
for every eligible U cell,
record:

favored-side local core field Q_favored;
opposing-side local core field Q_opposing;
base lambda to the adverse side;
gated lambda to the adverse side;
whether the cell recruited;
which side it joined.

For MARGIN_EXCLUSION,
Q uses veteran M_pre.

For OCCUPANCY_EXCLUSION,
Q uses committed occupancy only.

Report:

mean and median Q_favored;
fraction Q_favored > 0;
mean base adverse lambda;
mean gated adverse lambda;
fractional adverse-lambda suppression;
adverse-side recruitment rate.

Also stratify adverse-side recruitment
by Q_favored quartile.

The high-Q quartile
should recruit to the adverse side less often
than the low-Q quartile
if the field is mechanistically active.

CORE-ADJACENT REBUILD METRIC

At each biased adverse-pulse onset,
freeze the favored-side committed survivor-core identities.

During that adverse burst,
measure the fraction of U recruitment events
within radius 3 of those core cells
that join the adverse side.

Report separately for:

BASE;
OCCUPANCY_EXCLUSION;
MARGIN_EXCLUSION.

This is the direct macro-mechanism diagnostic.

CORE SURVIVAL

Preserve A40 core-persistence reporting
after adverse epochs 1, 2, and 3.

A41 does not claim success
merely because the original core survives.

The key question is whether
opposing recruitment around it is reduced enough
to prevent population-level cycle closure.

TRUE REVERSAL COST

Preserve:

reversal acquisition;
old-majority loss latency;
new-majority acquisition;
median old-side M at reversal onset;
median M-to-zero latency;
signed B zero-cross latency.

Additionally report:

time from reversal onset
until opposing-side recruitment
within radius 3 of the old core
returns to at least the BASE arm's
same-context median recruitment rate.

This detects stale spatial exclusion.

PRIMARY POPULATION METRICS

For every arm report:

aggregate service;
harm rate;
overall oscillation;
biased-periodic oscillation;
balanced false-majority;
false C dominance;
false S dominance;
contradiction no-majority;
reversal acquisition;
median old-majority loss;
directional coordination;
H occupancy;
niche prevalence;
recruitment activity.

A41 MARGIN-EXCLUSION QUALIFICATION

D2_MARGIN_EXCLUSION or D3_MARGIN_EXCLUSION
is A41-QUALIFIED iff all are true:

1. overall oscillation <= 5%;

2. biased-periodic oscillation <= 10%;

3. breaks at least 50%
   of paired BASE biased-periodic oscillators;

4. biased-periodic oscillation
   is lower than paired OCCUPANCY_EXCLUSION;

5. balanced false-majority <= 10%;

6. false C dominance
   does not exceed paired BASE;

7. false S dominance
   does not exceed paired BASE;

8. reversal acquisition >= 80%;

9. median old-majority loss <= 4 epochs;

10. aggregate service >= 90%
    of paired BASE;

11. recruitment remains nondegenerate;

12. high-Q adverse-side recruitment rate
    is lower than low-Q rate;

13. core-adjacent adverse rebuild
    is lower than paired BASE;

14. all integrity probes pass.

A41_INFORMATION_GAIN

TRUE iff at least one MARGIN_EXCLUSION arm:

reduces biased-periodic oscillation
versus paired BASE;

breaks at least 25%
of paired BASE biased-periodic oscillators;

reduces core-adjacent adverse rebuild
versus paired BASE;

shows lower adverse recruitment
in the high-Q quartile than the low-Q quartile;

retains reversal acquisition >= 80%;

retains >= 90% paired BASE service;

and balanced false-majority remains <= 10%.

CAUSAL ATTRIBUTION

If MARGIN_EXCLUSION succeeds
and OCCUPANCY_EXCLUSION does not:

evidence-depth-weighted veteran topology matters,
not merely incumbent density.

If both succeed similarly:

spatial incumbent topology matters,
but accumulated evidence depth
adds little beyond occupancy.

If both reduce local adverse rebuild
but macro oscillation remains:

population turnover near the core
is not the remaining oscillator bottleneck.

If MARGIN_EXCLUSION stops oscillation
but becomes sticky on true reversal:

the spatial field persists too strongly
and must later acquire a local release mechanism.

If neither changes adverse recruitment:

the survivor core is too sparse
or too weakly positioned
to control recruitment topology.

